P3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17699, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MXGvhtz5X6PzazLc1HMNae", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 at detection; v2.3.1 marked unhealthy in production). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), leaving the service mixed across versions; I retried the same rollback, which completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause before re-releasing, and look into the orchestrator partial failure during rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48299, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MXGvhtz5X6PzazLc1HMNae", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48299, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MXGvhtz5X6PzazLc1HMNae", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49367, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QMGeN6eeKR7ihQ4bS5yKMb", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49667, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QMGeN6eeKR7ihQ4bS5yKMb", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null,